body:
Coordinator, merge note for head 7cdb8b8d94a8329ad250bc4853ec5a6ea4f6891f. Class: no refresh (the head is the reviewed head). The maintainer ordered the merge of the ready PRs on 2026-11-22.

This merge relies on:
- two collaborator reviews of this head: the read of 2026-11-20 (the three earlier findings are met) and the review of 19:45Z with a built trial merge ("Ready for the maintainer to merge");
- the screenshots (before and after) in the PR body;
- a trial merge here, on `main` a181bf1f3 with this head (the merge is clean): the whole quick plan, 28 steps, 0 failed: `sim` lib 232 passed, `sim_op_steps` 9, `arc_plane` 3; the app suites `sim` 4, `sim_op_step_stock` 2, `stock_play` 8, `posting` 17, `first_traverse` 4; the 16 ui steps, with `ui suites: lib` 1466 passed and 8 ignored. Clippy is clean on `camcraft-sim`, `camcraft-motion` and `camcraft-ui` with all targets, and on the `camcraft-app` lib.
- The heavy lanes are not a merge condition (#3556). The contributor ran them on this head (233 of 234 steps). The review of 19:45Z says that the one red step of that run passes on the current trial merge.

Not run: the light lane (its two twins test `camcraft-motion` code, which this PR does not change), and the steps of the batch plan that the diff does not touch.

`main` moved after the trial by #3353 (2D Offset pass start). GitHub reports that this head merges with the new `main`.

@vilts thank you for this feature and for the tests.
